  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Art Illustration Festival: Scene gift boxes (宝可梦艺术插画庆典 景) came out on 28 June 2024, postponed from 31 May, in two versions, a Poké Ball box and an Ultra Ball box, the Ultra Ball's first time as a box; each ball can be kept for storage or display. Each box held one art illustration holo, one of nine whose different art styles bring each artist's character to the card: Oricorio, Toxtricity, Galarian Articuno, Mew, Deoxys, Galarian Zapdos, Galarian Moltres, Altaria and Latias. It also held a Poké Ball or Ultra Ball holo card, which with luck was replaced by a random special-art Trainer holo, and a random 25-card Nine Colours Gathering pack.\n\nThe nine art cards are numbered out of 11 with the Ultra Ball and Poké Ball cards; the special-art Trainers Kabu, Bea, Gordie, Milo and Nessa are numbered past it, up to 016.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: The Poké Ball and Ultra Ball gift boxes: Pokémon Art Illustration Festival, Scene (8 June 2024)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/product/15840.html"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: Release of the Art Illustration Festival Scene gift boxes postponed (23 May 2024)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/other/17157.html"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"CSJC\" mark at the bottom left, and a number out of 011",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: The Poké Ball and Ultra Ball gift boxes: Pokémon Art Illustration Festival, Scene (8 June 2024)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/product/15840.html"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: Release of the Art Illustration Festival Scene gift boxes postponed (23 May 2024)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/other/17157.html"
      }
    ]
  },
